                Most colour disputes are not colour disputes. They are file
                disputes that surface later, when a line is too thin to hold
                enamel or a font has quietly changed shape on someone else's
                machine. A production-ready file is not a beautiful file; it is a
                file with no remaining decisions in it.
              </p>

